    "summaryAr": "About Omni Omni is the AI analytics platform that turns company data into a trusted source of truth for AI. Built on a semantic model, Omni gives enterprises a governed context graph for analytics and AI. Teams use Omni to ask questions in plain English, refine answers in workbooks, and bring trusted data into tools like Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, and Slack. Based in San Francisco, CA, Omni has raised $217M from the wo",
    "descriptionAr": "About Omni Omni is the AI analytics platform that turns company data into a trusted source of truth for AI. Built on a semantic model, Omni gives enterprises a governed context graph for analytics and AI. Teams use Omni to ask questions in plain English, refine answers in workbooks, and bring trusted data into tools like Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, and Slack. Based in San Francisco, CA, Omni has raised $217M from the world’s top investors, including ICONIQ, Theory Ventures, First Round Capital, Redpoint Ventures, and GV. Its latest $120M Series C valued the company at $1.5B. The Role We're looking for a Frontend Engineer to build the product experiences customers use every day to explore, visualize, and share their data in Omni. You'll own meaningful features from design through delivery, shipping fast, polished, and intuitive interfaces across the product, including the surfaces customers use to embed Omni in their own applications. You'll partner closely with product, design, and engineers across the stack, and work directly with customers to understand how they use Omni. This is a high-autonomy role for someone who can take ownership of large areas of the frontend with minimal oversight. Responsibilities Own features across Omni's frontend end-to-end: technical decisions, implementation, and delivery Partner directly with customers and the product team to scope integration requirements Design and build the APIs, SDKs, and front-end surfaces that let companies embed Omni in their own products Move quickly and ship iteratively, refining based on customer feedback Use AI coding tools (e.g., Claude Code) to maximize velocity and focus on the highest-leverage technical work Collaborate with engineers across the stack as needed, without requiring day-to-day oversight Represent Embed customer needs in broader product and engineering planning About You 5+ years of software engineering experience, including 2+ years operating at a senior level and shipping production software independently Strong proficiency in JavaScript and TypeScript Proven track record delivering senior-level projects to customers Experience with data or business intelligence tools or applications (e.g., SQL, Looker, Tableau, Mode, Amplitude, Google Analytics) Demonstrated bias to action — comfortable making decisions and shipping with limited oversight Proficiency with AI coding tools and workflows (e.g., Claude Code, Cursor) Experience building and maintaining APIs or SDKs consumed by external customers Nice to Haves Startup experience Working confidence in Java or Python Experience building SaaS applications that run in the cloud Tech Stack JavaScript / TypeScript HTML / CSS Java, Python (a plus, not required) Location This role is based in San Francisco, or remote for candidates based near one of Omni's engineering hubs (Philadelphia, Boulder/Denver, Santa Cruz, or Seattle); final-round interviews are conducted in person. Why Join Us Passionate, supportive team with extensive experience in the space (including founders from Looker and Stitch Data) all working together to win as a team Health, dental, and vision insurance 401(k) Plan (for US-based roles) Unlimited PTO Omni is an equal opportunity employer. We value diversity and encourage you to apply even if you don’t check every single box. Please, let us know if you need any reasonable accommodations during the interview process.",
